# graph_agents — the agent fleet.
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored, and do not add them:
#   .claude/        the agents and skills ARE the product of this repo
#   .graph/runs/    run state is the fleet's memory; it is small and it is history

# Python bytecode (the hooks are stdlib Python)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# OS cruft
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# portfolio/registry.json is untracked on purpose: its path/entry_docs fields
# name real app directories on disk (personal names among them). It still
# exists locally and the fleet still reads it for routing — it is just not
# published.
#
# CONSEQUENCE, and it is not obvious: a fresh clone of this repo has NO registry.
# `scout.md` step 1 and `feature-graph` step 1 both make it the mandatory first
# read, so routing fails on a clone with no visible reason. Rebuild it before the
# first run — see CURRENT-STATE.md § "What is live", the registry row.
portfolio/registry.json

# Live session state written by the harness, not by the fleet. Holds a pid.
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# A pointer to the run currently open, written by `feature-graph` step 1 so that
# hooks — which get a file path and an agent_type, never a run id — can find the
# run's state. Machine-local and disposable: a pointer to a closed run is ignored,
# and a clone with no pointer simply has no open run.
.graph/CURRENT
